From d8ceabcfd06b3759c99eef9149c90ad91306e467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/20] feat(deployment): key deployment runs by generation

A spec change while a service was being deployed was absorbed: the
next round followed the single deployment:{uid} run, whose inputs carry
the old spec, and wrote Ready with the new observedGeneration. An
accelerator change while Preparing looped on AllocationFailed, because
the first-fit scheduler refuses to reuse a held allocation that no
longer fits and nothing released it.

Deployment runs, and the instances they launch, are now keyed by uid
and generation (deployment:{uid}:{generation}). find_deployment_runs
looks up every run of a resource through the find_runs prefix lookup,
including runs started before 1.1.0 under deployment:{uid}, so the
releaser still cancels in-flight runs and stops every instance when the
resource is deleted.

Before starting a run the reconciler stops the previous deployment
through the release provider, so only one instance uses the allocated
devices. In Deploying or Verifying without a run for the current
generation it stops the old run and starts one for the new spec without
a phase change. When the scheduler refuses to reuse the allocation held
for an earlier generation, the reconciler stops the instances, releases
that allocation and allocates again. A failure to stop the previous
deployment backs off like a failed start (StopFailed).
